{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-Met/uma-sim/pulls/116","id":4791810172,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUMqmY88AAAABHZ04fA","html_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-Met/uma-sim/pull/116","diff_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-Met/uma-sim/pull/116.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-Met/uma-sim/pull/116.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-Met/uma-sim/issues/116","number":116,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Keep browser career actions bound to the displayed session","user":{"login":"Jacob-Met","id":150724801,"node_id":"U_kgDOCPvgwQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/150724801?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met","html_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-Met","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Switching careers while an action or refresh is delayed can replace the selected view with an earlier career's state, text or error. Run actions also follow the server's mutable active-session default, so another client can redirect an action away from the career currently displayed.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Retain the displayed session for actions, auto-step, fast-forward, deck placement, style changes, follow-up reads and telemetry exports.\n- Give each request ownership of its result, error and busy cleanup. Selecting a session, starting again or unmounting retires obsolete completions; a synchronous guard prevents duplicate run submissions.\n- Preserve the distinction between an omitted selector (active session) and an explicit empty selector (main session) in the browser URL helper and the three native API selector functions.\n- Match number shortcuts to visible choices and suppress them on the Library tab, in editable fields, or during modified/repeated/composition input.\n- Retain current Conditions/Skills panels, event/race history, lab behavior, all existing tests and Playwright. Add the focused session tests to the existing package scripts and adapt their compiler to the current component CSS imports.\n\n## Receiving and source review\n\nCurrent-main parent: `8d74413d7dbc3caf1745779c92d56b6eb7feea42`. Published head: `63aca264ee8b47df14bcecf47cf1b390b244852f`; tree: `ebf0e447639c24b30d364dea0c5a92a5f6d9966b`. This normal merge retains the original qualified contribution and its native evidence as ancestors. All 1,536 unrelated incoming leaves and all 28 intended changes/additions were read back and verified.\n\n| Gate | Actual result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Current native `npm run build` | 101 tests passed, TypeScript passed, Vite built 68 modules; all 63 input files preserved |\n| Independent current React receiving | 20/20 passed, including App → Lab → Activate → Run with a delayed old action and current-panel state/history checks |\n| Independent current wrapper HTTP capture | 39 cases / 60 real local HTTP requests passed for unchanged MCP/TUI selector serialization |\n| Original native qualification | 5 new session tests and 12 existing API tests passed; full workspace 344 passed on the historical qualified tree |\n| Current full hosted Rust/browser/CI | Pending; retained as required merge gates |\n\nComplete current build output, input/dist hashes, exact independent receiver and source review are in `docs/qualification/browser-session-20261008/current-receiving/`. The original native log is preserved separately with its exact historical source attribution. An initial shared-disk ENOSPC refusal is retained beside the later successful identical-source build; it is not counted as a product test pass.\n\nThis retires obsolete UI completions; it does not cancel an action already accepted by the server or make multiple reads of the same session transactional. No installed service or deployment changed.\n\nCloses #63.","created_at":"2026-10-08T19:30:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T19:30:06Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1a5f06b48e49e9d6fe43583dea1b57cbd4d2f8e8","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-Met/uma-sim/pulls/116/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-Met/uma-sim/pulls/116/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-Met/uma-sim/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-Met/uma-sim/issues/116/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-Met/uma-sim/statuses/63aca264ee8b47df14bcecf47cf1b390b244852f","head":{"label":"Jacob-Met:production/session-ui-69570d292200","ref":"production/session-ui-69570d292200","sha":"63aca264ee8b47df14bcecf47cf1b390b244852f","user":{"login":"Jacob-Met","id":150724801,"node_id":"U_kgDOCPvgwQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/150724801?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met","html_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-Met","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-Met/orgs","repos_url":"h